---
id: AP-005
type: rule
family: guardrail-suppression
title: '@ts-expect-error used'
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 3

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx]
allowlist: ['**/*.test.ts', '**/*.spec.ts', '**/__tests__/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '@ts-expect-error'

related: [AP-004]
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

This type error is being suppressed rather than fixed. Read the error
message and resolve the type mismatch if possible.

If suppression is genuinely necessary, `@ts-expect-error` is the right
choice — it will fail when the underlying issue is resolved. Ensure the
comment explains exactly why this case can't satisfy the type system.
